  ('N10.6-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'An agent notices a typo in the purchase price that favors their client by $10,000. The ethical step is:', '["Wait until after closing","Say nothing because it benefits the client","Point out the error so the documents reflect the actual agreement","Tell only the client"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Honesty and fair dealing mean correcting known errors.', '["Waiting makes the problem worse.","Taking advantage of a known mistake isn''t honest dealing.","","The documents must reflect the real agreement for everyone."]'::jsonb, 'Honest with everyone.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'fairness-all-parties-ethics', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Relying on verbal agreements for repairs reduces risk because there''s less paperwork to get wrong.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Verbal agreements are hard to prove. Put agreements in writing.",""]'::jsonb, 'Write it down.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'verbal-agreements-risk', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'A home sells for $485,000 at a 6% commission. The listing brokerage gets half. The listing salesperson gets 60% of the listing brokerage''s share. How much does the listing salesperson receive?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":8730,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Split in steps: total, then brokerage, then salesperson: $8,730.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Price times rate, then split, then split again.', 'Salesperson = price × rate × brokerage share × salesperson split', '["Total commission: $485,000 × 0.06 = $29,100.","Listing brokerage: $29,100 × 0.5 = $14,550.","Salesperson: $14,550 × 0.6 = $8,730."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-commission-two-splits', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'A seller wants to net $310,000 after paying a 6% commission and $4,500 in closing costs. What is the lowest sale price that achieves this? (Round to the nearest dollar.)', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":334574,"tolerance":1,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Divide what the seller needs by the 94% left after commission: about $334,574.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Need a net? Divide by what''s left after commission.', 'Price = (desired net + costs) ÷ (1 − commission rate)', '["Net plus costs: $310,000 + $4,500 = $314,500.","1 − 0.06 = 0.94.","$314,500 ÷ 0.94 ≈ $334,574."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-price-for-net', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A broker earned a $16,250 commission on a $325,000 sale. What was the commission rate, in percent?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":5,"tolerance":0,"unit":"%"}'::jsonb, '$16,250 is 5% of $325,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Part ÷ whole = rate.', 'Rate = commission ÷ price × 100', '["$16,250 ÷ $325,000 = 0.05.","0.05 × 100 = 5%."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-find-rate', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A 6% commission came to $21,000. What was the sale price?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":350000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '$21,000 ÷ 0.06 = $350,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Part ÷ rate = whole.', 'Price = commission ÷ rate', '["$21,000 ÷ 0.06 = $350,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-find-price-from-commission', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A home sells for $390,000. The seller pays a 5.5% commission, $3,200 in other costs, and a $210,000 loan payoff. What is the seller''s net?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":155350,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Subtract every seller cost: $155,350.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Price minus everything the seller pays.', 'Net = price − commission − costs − payoff', '["Commission: $390,000 × 0.055 = $21,450.","$390,000 − $21,450 − $3,200 − $210,000 = $155,350."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-sellers-net', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A listing pays 7% on the first $100,000 of the price and 3% on the rest. The home sells for $350,000. What is the commission?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":14500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Add the two tiers: $14,500.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Tier by tier, then add.', 'Commission = (first tier × rate 1) + (remainder × rate 2)', '["First $100,000 × 0.07 = $7,000.","Remaining $250,000 × 0.03 = $7,500.","$7,000 + $7,500 = $14,500."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-tiered-commission', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A $400,000 sale pays a 5% commission, split equally between the listing and selling brokerages. The selling salesperson gets 70% of their brokerage''s share. How much does the selling salesperson receive?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":7000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '70% of the selling side''s $10,000 is $7,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Price times rate, then split, then split again.', 'Salesperson = price × rate × side share × split', '["Total: $400,000 × 0.05 = $20,000.","Selling side: $20,000 × 0.5 = $10,000.","Salesperson: $10,000 × 0.7 = $7,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-selling-side-salesperson', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'calculation', 'The commission is 6%, split 50/50 between brokerages, and the salesperson gets 50% of their brokerage''s share. What percent of the sale price does the salesperson receive?', '["1.5%","3%","0.75%","6%"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '6% × 0.5 × 0.5 = 1.5% of the price.', '["","3% is the brokerage''s share before the salesperson split.","That halves one time too many.","6% is the total commission."]'::jsonb, 'Multiply the percentages through.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-salesperson-percent-of-price', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which formula finds the sale price a seller needs to reach a desired net?', '["Desired net + (desired net × rate)","(Desired net + costs) ÷ (1 − commission rate)","Desired net × commission rate","(Desired net − costs) × (1 + rate)"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'The commission comes out of the price, so divide by the share the seller keeps.', '["Adding commission on the net underestimates the price.","","That gives a commission amount, not a price.","Subtracting costs and multiplying is backward."]'::jsonb, 'Need a net? Divide by what''s left after commission.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-net-formula', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.1-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A sales commission is normally calculated on the loan amount.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Points are on the loan; commissions are on the price.', '["Commissions are calculated on the sale price, unless the agreement says otherwise.",""]'::jsonb, 'Points on the loan, commission on the price.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-commission-on-price', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'Annual property taxes of $3,960 are paid in arrears. Closing is March 15, and the seller owns the day of closing. Using a 360-day year, how much does the seller owe the buyer for taxes?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":825,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The seller owes 75 days of unpaid tax: $825, a seller debit and buyer credit.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Daily amount × days owed.', 'Proration = (annual tax ÷ 360) × days the seller owned', '["Daily tax: $3,960 ÷ 360 = $11.","Seller''s days: January (30) + February (30) + 15 days of March = 75.","75 × $11 = $825."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-proration-taxes-arrears-360', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'The seller collected $1,800 rent for June. Closing is June 20, and the seller owns the day of closing. Using a 30-day month, how much rent does the seller credit the buyer?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":600,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The buyer is owed the 10 days after closing: $600.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Whoever used it or kept it pays for it.', 'Credit = (monthly rent ÷ 30) × buyer''s days', '["Daily rent: $1,800 ÷ 30 = $60.","Buyer owns June 21–30: 10 days.","10 × $60 = $600."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-proration-rent-30-day', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'Annual taxes are $4,380, paid in arrears. Closing is April 10 in a non-leap year, and the seller owns the day of closing. Using a 365-day year, how much does the seller owe?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":1200,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '100 days at $12 is $1,200.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Know which calendar: 360 or 365.', 'Proration = (annual tax ÷ 365) × actual days', '["Daily: $4,380 ÷ 365 = $12.","Days: Jan 31 + Feb 28 + Mar 31 + Apr 10 = 100.","100 × $12 = $1,200."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-proration-365', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'The seller prepaid $540 in HOA dues for July through September. Closing is August 10, and the seller owns the day of closing. Using 30-day months, how much does the buyer owe the seller?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":300,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The seller prepaid days the buyer will use: $300 to the seller.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Prepaid by the seller? The buyer pays them back.', 'Credit to seller = (prepaid amount ÷ days covered) × buyer''s days', '["Daily: $540 ÷ 90 = $6.","Buyer''s days: August 11–30 (20) + September (30) = 50.","50 × $6 = $300."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-proration-prepaid-hoa', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Property taxes are paid in arrears. On the closing statement, the seller''s share appears as:', '["A debit to the seller and a credit to the buyer","A credit to the seller and a debit to the buyer","A debit to both","A credit to both"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The buyer will pay the whole bill later, so the seller credits the buyer for the seller''s days.', '["","That''s the entry for an item the seller prepaid.","Only one party owes it.","No one receives it twice."]'::jsonb, 'Arrears: seller pays the buyer.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-arrears-entry', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'The seller collected rent in advance for the month of closing. The buyer''s share of that rent is:', '["A debit to the seller and a credit to the buyer","Ignored","Paid to the tenant","A credit to the seller and a debit to the buyer"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The seller holds rent for days after closing, so the seller pays the buyer.', '["","It must be prorated.","The tenant already paid.","The seller kept money belonging to the buyer''s days."]'::jsonb, 'Whoever used it or kept it pays for it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-rent-advance-entry', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'A buyer assumes a $120,000 loan at 6%. Interest is paid in arrears. Closing is on the 15th, and the seller owes interest for 15 days. Using a 30-day month, how much interest does the seller owe?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":300,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The seller owes 15 days of accrued interest: $300.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Arrears: seller pays the buyer.', 'Interest = (balance × rate ÷ 12 ÷ 30) × days', '["Monthly interest: $120,000 × 0.06 ÷ 12 = $600.","Daily: $600 ÷ 30 = $20.","15 × $20 = $300."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-proration-assumed-interest', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A 360-day year treats every month as 30 days.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","That''s the banker''s year convention."]'::jsonb, '360 means 30-day months.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-360-30-day-months', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'The seller prepaid an item that covers days after closing. The buyer''s portion is:', '["A credit to the seller and a debit to the buyer","A debit to the seller and a credit to the buyer","Paid by the lender","Refunded by the county"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The buyer reimburses the seller for the prepaid days the buyer will enjoy.', '["","That''s the entry for arrears items.","The lender isn''t involved.","No refund comes from the county."]'::jsonb, 'Prepaid by the seller? The buyer pays them back.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-prepaid-entry', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.2-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'Annual property taxes are $2,700. What is the monthly amount for proration purposes?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":225,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '$2,700 ÷ 12 = $225.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Annual ÷ 12 = monthly.', 'Monthly = annual ÷ 12', '["$2,700 ÷ 12 = $225."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-monthly-tax', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'What is the first month''s interest on a $250,000 loan at 6.6% annual interest?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":1375,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Annual interest of $16,500 divided by 12 is $1,375.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Annual interest ÷ 12.', 'Monthly interest = loan × annual rate ÷ 12', '["$250,000 × 0.066 = $16,500 a year.","$16,500 ÷ 12 = $1,375."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-first-month-interest', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A $240,000 loan at 6% has a monthly principal and interest payment of $1,580. How much of the first payment goes to principal?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":380,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Whatever isn''t interest reduces principal: $380.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Annual interest ÷ 12, then the rest hits principal.', 'Principal = payment − (balance × rate ÷ 12)', '["First month''s interest: $240,000 × 0.06 ÷ 12 = $1,200.","$1,580 − $1,200 = $380."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-principal-portion', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'Using the same loan ($240,000 at 6%, $1,580 payment), what is the balance after the first payment?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":239620,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Only the principal portion reduces the balance: $239,620.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Only principal lowers the balance.', 'New balance = old balance − principal paid', '["Interest: $1,200; principal: $380.","$240,000 − $380 = $239,620."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-balance-after-payment', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'How much simple interest is due on $15,000 borrowed at 8% for 9 months?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":900,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '$15,000 × 8% × ¾ year = $900.', '[]'::jsonb, 'I = P × R × T.', 'Interest = principal × rate × time (in years)', '["9 months = 0.75 year.","$15,000 × 0.08 × 0.75 = $900."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-simple-interest-months', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A lender offers 85% LTV on a home appraised and priced at $410,000. What is the maximum loan?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":348500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '85% of $410,000 is $348,500.', '[]'::jsonb, 'LTV: loan over value.', 'Loan = value × LTV', '["$410,000 × 0.85 = $348,500."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-loan-from-ltv', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A borrower pays 2.25 points on a $320,000 loan. How much do the points cost?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":7200,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '2.25% of the loan is $7,200.', '[]'::jsonb, 'A point is 1% of the loan, not the price.', 'Cost = loan × points ÷ 100', '["2.25 points = 0.0225.","$320,000 × 0.0225 = $7,200."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-points-decimal', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'Monthly principal and interest is $1,850. Annual property taxes are $3,000, and annual homeowner''s insurance is $1,440. What is the monthly PITI?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":2220,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Add monthly taxes and insurance to P&I: $2,220.', '[]'::jsonb, 'PITI: principal, interest, taxes, insurance.', 'PITI = P&I + (annual taxes ÷ 12) + (annual insurance ÷ 12)', '["Taxes: $3,000 ÷ 12 = $250.","Insurance: $1,440 ÷ 12 = $120.","$1,850 + $250 + $120 = $2,220."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-piti', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A payment table shows $6.00 per $1,000 borrowed per month. What is the monthly payment on a $275,000 loan?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":1650,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '275 thousands at $6 each is $1,650.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Thousands times the factor.', 'Payment = (loan ÷ 1,000) × factor', '["$275,000 ÷ 1,000 = 275.","275 × $6.00 = $1,650."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-payment-factor', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A borrower paid $1,125 in interest for one month on a $225,000 balance. What is the annual interest rate, in percent?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":6,"tolerance":0,"unit":"%"}'::jsonb, '$13,500 a year on $225,000 is 6%.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Annualize, then divide.', 'Rate = (monthly interest × 12) ÷ balance × 100', '["Annual interest: $1,125 × 12 = $13,500.","$13,500 ÷ $225,000 = 0.06 = 6%."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-find-interest-rate', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.3-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'For the same loan amount and rate, which choice increases the total interest paid over the life of the loan?', '["A larger down payment","A shorter loan term","A longer loan term","Extra principal payments"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Spreading payments over more years means paying interest for longer.', '["Borrowing less reduces interest.","Shorter terms reduce total interest.","","Paying principal early reduces interest."]'::jsonb, 'Longer loan, more interest.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-longer-term-more-interest', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A home bought for $280,000 is now worth $336,000. What is the percent appreciation?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":20,"tolerance":0,"unit":"%"}'::jsonb, 'A $56,000 gain on $280,000 is 20%.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Change over original.', 'Percent change = (new − old) ÷ old × 100', '["$336,000 − $280,000 = $56,000.","$56,000 ÷ $280,000 = 0.20 = 20%."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-appreciation-percent', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A $400,000 home appreciates 4% a year, compounded, for 2 years. What is it worth after 2 years?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":432640,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Each year''s growth builds on the last: $432,640.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Multiply year by year.', 'Value = original × (1 + rate) for each year', '["Year 1: $400,000 × 1.04 = $416,000.","Year 2: $416,000 × 1.04 = $432,640."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-compound-appreciation', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'An investor bought a lot for $300,000 and sold it for $270,000. What was the percent loss?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":10,"tolerance":0,"unit":"%"}'::jsonb, 'A $30,000 loss on $300,000 is 10%.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Change over original.', 'Percent change = (old − new) ÷ old × 100', '["$300,000 − $270,000 = $30,000.","$30,000 ÷ $300,000 = 0.10 = 10%."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-percent-loss', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'An investor pays $250,000 cash for a rental that produces $15,000 net income a year. What is the annual return on investment, in percent?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":6,"tolerance":0,"unit":"%"}'::jsonb, '$15,000 on $250,000 is a 6% return.', '[]'::jsonb, 'IRV: cover what you need.', 'ROI = net income ÷ investment × 100', '["$15,000 ÷ $250,000 = 0.06 = 6%."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-roi-cash', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A building''s NOI is $52,000, and the market cap rate is 6.5%. What is its value?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":800000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Income ÷ rate = $800,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'IRV: Income ÷ Rate = Value.', 'Value = NOI ÷ cap rate', '["$52,000 ÷ 0.065 = $800,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-value-from-cap', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A property valued at $600,000 at a 7% cap rate produces what annual NOI?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":42000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Value × rate = income: $42,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'IRV: Rate × Value = Income.', 'NOI = value × cap rate', '["$600,000 × 0.07 = $42,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-noi-from-cap', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'For tax purposes, residential rental buildings are depreciated over 27.5 years. A building (excluding land) cost $330,000. What is the annual depreciation deduction, using straight-line?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":12000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '$330,000 spread over 27.5 years is $12,000 a year.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Buildings depreciate; land doesn''t.', 'Annual depreciation = building cost ÷ 27.5', '["$330,000 ÷ 27.5 = $12,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-tax-depreciation-275', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A commercial property sold for $1,800,000 with annual gross income of $200,000. What is its gross income multiplier?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":9,"tolerance":0,"unit":""}'::jsonb, 'The price is 9 times annual gross income.', '[]'::jsonb, 'GRM monthly, GIM yearly.', 'GIM = price ÷ annual gross income', '["$1,800,000 ÷ $200,000 = 9."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-gim-calc', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'An investor sold a home for $378,000, making an 8% profit on the purchase price. What did the investor pay?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":350000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The sale price is 108% of cost, so divide by 1.08: $350,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Profit on cost: divide by 1 plus the rate.', 'Original cost = sale price ÷ (1 + profit rate)', '["1 + 0.08 = 1.08.","$378,000 ÷ 1.08 = $350,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-original-cost-from-profit', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.4-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'If a property''s NOI rises 10% and the cap rate doesn''t change, its value:', '["Rises 10%","Rises 20%","Stays the same","Falls 10%"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Value = NOI ÷ rate, so value rises in the same proportion as NOI.', '["","Value rises by the same percent as NOI.","Changing income changes value.","Value moves with income at a fixed rate."]'::jsonb, 'Income up, value up.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-noi-up-value-up', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A rectangular parcel measures 150 feet by 580.8 feet. How many acres is it?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":2,"tolerance":0.001,"unit":"acres"}'::jsonb, '87,120 square feet is exactly 2 acres.', '[]'::jsonb, '43,560 makes an acre.', 'Acres = (length × width) ÷ 43,560', '["150 × 580.8 = 87,120 sq ft.","87,120 ÷ 43,560 = 2 acres."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-acres-rectangle', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A triangular lot has a 200-foot base and a 150-foot height. What is its area in square feet?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":15000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"sq ft"}'::jsonb, 'Half of base times height is 15,000 sq ft.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Triangle: half of base times height.', 'Triangle area = ½ × base × height', '["200 × 150 = 30,000.","30,000 ÷ 2 = 15,000 sq ft."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-triangle-area', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A room is 15 feet by 18 feet. How many square yards is it?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":30,"tolerance":0,"unit":"sq yd"}'::jsonb, '270 square feet is 30 square yards.', '[]'::jsonb, '9 square feet make a square yard.', 'Square yards = square feet ÷ 9', '["15 × 18 = 270 sq ft.","270 ÷ 9 = 30 sq yd."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-square-yards', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'Carpet costs $40 per square yard installed. How much will it cost to carpet a 12 ft by 21 ft room?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":1120,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '28 square yards at $40 is $1,120.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Convert first, then price it.', 'Cost = (square feet ÷ 9) × price per square yard', '["12 × 21 = 252 sq ft.","252 ÷ 9 = 28 sq yd.","28 × $40 = $1,120."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-carpet-cost', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'An L-shaped building is made of a 40 ft by 30 ft section and a 20 ft by 15 ft section. What is its total area?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":1500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"sq ft"}'::jsonb, 'Split the shape into rectangles and add: 1,500 sq ft.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Break it into rectangles.', 'Total area = sum of the rectangles', '["40 × 30 = 1,200 sq ft.","20 × 15 = 300 sq ft.","1,200 + 300 = 1,500 sq ft."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-l-shape-area', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'A driveway slab is 60 ft long, 12 ft wide, and 6 inches thick. How many cubic yards of concrete are needed? (Round to two decimals.)', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":13.33,"tolerance":0.01,"unit":"cu yd"}'::jsonb, '360 cubic feet is about 13.33 cubic yards.', '[]'::jsonb, '27 cubic feet in a cubic yard.', 'Cubic yards = (length × width × thickness in feet) ÷ 27', '["6 inches = 0.5 ft.","60 × 12 × 0.5 = 360 cu ft.","360 ÷ 27 ≈ 13.33 cu yd."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-concrete-cubic-yards', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A lot is 75 feet wide along the street and 140 feet deep. It sells for $1,800 per front foot. What is the price?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":135000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Price by frontage only: 75 × $1,800 = $135,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Front first.', 'Price = front feet × price per front foot', '["Front feet = 75.","75 × $1,800 = $135,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-front-foot-price', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'How many square feet are in 2.5 acres?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":108900,"tolerance":0,"unit":"sq ft"}'::jsonb, '2.5 acres is 108,900 square feet.', '[]'::jsonb, '43,560 makes an acre.', 'Square feet = acres × 43,560', '["2.5 × 43,560 = 108,900 sq ft."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-acres-to-sqft', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A 5-acre parcel sells for $175,000. What is the price per acre?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":35000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '$175,000 ÷ 5 acres = $35,000 an acre.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Total ÷ units = per unit.', 'Price per acre = price ÷ acres', '["$175,000 ÷ 5 = $35,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-price-per-acre', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.5-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'A rectangular quarter-acre lot is 90 feet wide. How deep is it, in feet?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":121,"tolerance":0,"unit":"feet"}'::jsonb, 'A quarter acre is 10,890 sq ft; divided by 90 ft wide is 121 ft deep.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Area ÷ one side = the other side.', 'Depth = (acres × 43,560) ÷ width', '["0.25 × 43,560 = 10,890 sq ft.","10,890 ÷ 90 = 121 ft."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-lot-depth-quarter-acre', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A property''s assessed value is $120,000, and the tax rate is 3.2%. What is the annual tax?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":3840,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '3.2% of $120,000 is $3,840.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Assessed value × rate.', 'Tax = assessed value × rate', '["$120,000 × 0.032 = $3,840."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-tax-percent', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'Assessed value is $150,000, and the tax rate is 25 mills. What is the annual tax?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":3750,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '25 mills is $25 per $1,000: $3,750.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Per mill, divide by 1,000.', 'Tax = assessed value × (mills ÷ 1,000)', '["25 mills = 25 ÷ 1,000 = 0.025.","$150,000 × 0.025 = $3,750."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-tax-mills', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'Assessed value is $98,000, and the rate is $3.66 per $100. What is the annual tax?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":3586.8,"tolerance":0.01,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '980 hundreds at $3.66 each is $3,586.80.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Per hundred, divide by 100.', 'Tax = (assessed value ÷ 100) × rate per $100', '["$98,000 ÷ 100 = 980.","980 × $3.66 = $3,586.80."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-tax-per-100', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'A home''s market value is $400,000. It''s assessed at 35% of market value, and the rate is $3.50 per $100 of assessed value. What is the annual tax?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":4900,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Find the assessed value first, then apply the rate: $4,900.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Assess first, then tax.', 'Tax = (market value × assessment ratio ÷ 100) × rate per $100', '["Assessed: $400,000 × 0.35 = $140,000.","$140,000 ÷ 100 = 1,400.","1,400 × $3.50 = $4,900."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-tax-assessment-ratio', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'A transfer tax is $2.00 for each $500 of price or fraction of $500. The price is $412,250. What is the tax?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":1650,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Round the partial unit up, then multiply: $1,650.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Count the units, then multiply.', 'Tax = (price ÷ 500, rounded up to the next whole unit) × rate', '["$412,250 ÷ 500 = 824.5 units.","A fraction counts as a full unit: 825.","825 × $2.00 = $1,650."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-transfer-tax-per-500', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A county charges a transfer tax of 0.5% of the sale price. What is the tax on a $360,000 sale?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":1800,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '0.5% of $360,000 is $1,800.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Price × rate.', 'Tax = price × rate', '["0.5% = 0.005.","$360,000 × 0.005 = $1,800."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-transfer-tax-percent', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 3, 'calculation', 'A district needs $2,000,000 in property tax revenue. The total assessed value in the district is $80,000,000. What tax rate is needed, in mills?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":25,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mills"}'::jsonb, 'The district needs 2.5%, which is 25 mills.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Per mill, divide by 1,000.', 'Rate = revenue needed ÷ total assessed value; mills = rate × 1,000', '["$2,000,000 ÷ $80,000,000 = 0.025.","0.025 × 1,000 = 25 mills."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-tax-rate-from-budget', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'One mill equals:', '["$0.10","$0.01","$1.00","$0.001"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'A mill is one-tenth of a cent.', '["That''s ten cents.","That''s one cent.","That''s a dollar.",""]'::jsonb, 'A mill is a tenth of a cent.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-mill-value', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'tf', 2, 'calculation', 'A tax rate of 3% is the same as 30 mills.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","3% = 0.03, and 0.03 × 1,000 = 30 mills."]'::jsonb, 'Percent × 10 = mills.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'math-mills-percent-conversion', 'unverified'),
  ('N11.6-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N11', 'N11.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A lender collects property taxes monthly in escrow. Annual taxes are $4,200. How much is collected each month?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":350,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '$4,200 a year is $350 a month.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Annual ÷ 12 = monthly.', 'Monthly escrow = annual tax ÷ 12', '["$4,200 ÷ 12 = $350."]'::jsonb, null, 'math-monthly-tax-escrow', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Which list contains the four government powers over private property?', '["Police power, eminent domain, taxation, escheat","Police power, partition, probate, escheat","Eminent domain, adverse possession, taxation, leasing","Zoning, appraisal, licensing, recording"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'PETE: Police power, Eminent domain, Taxation, Escheat.', '["","Partition and probate are court processes, not the four powers.","Adverse possession and leasing aren''t government powers.","Appraisal, licensing, and recording aren''t the four powers."]'::jsonb, 'PETE: Police, Eminent domain, Taxation, Escheat.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'pete-powers', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'When the government takes private land for a new highway, it must pay:', '["Only the assessed value","Only the owner''s mortgage balance","Nothing, under police power","Just compensation"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Eminent domain requires public use and just compensation.', '["Just compensation means fair market value, not assessed value.","The owner''s debt doesn''t set compensation.","Taking property requires payment.",""]'::jsonb, 'Take it for the public, pay for it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'eminent-domain-compensation', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'The legal process the government uses to exercise eminent domain is:', '["Foreclosure","Escheat","Condemnation","Partition"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Condemnation is how eminent domain is carried out.', '["Foreclosure enforces a lien.","Escheat is for property without heirs.","","Partition divides co-owned property."]'::jsonb, 'Condemn to take.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'condemnation-process', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A person dies without a will and with no heirs. Their land:', '["Is condemned","Escheats to the state","Goes to the nearest neighbor","Becomes public domain for anyone to claim"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'With no will and no heirs, property escheats to the state.', '["Condemnation is eminent domain.","","Neighbors have no claim.","It goes to the state, not to anyone."]'::jsonb, 'No heir? The state is the heir.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'escheat-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Zoning and building codes are examples of:', '["Taxation","Eminent domain, which requires compensation","Police power, which doesn''t require compensation","Escheat"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Police power lets government regulate for health and safety without paying owners.', '["Taxation is a separate power.","Regulating use isn''t taking title.","","Escheat is for property without heirs."]'::jsonb, 'Regulate, don''t pay.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'police-power-no-compensation', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A city installs new streetlights on one street and charges only the owners on that street. This is a:', '["Transfer tax","Escheat","Special assessment","General property tax"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Owners who benefit from a specific improvement pay a special assessment.', '["Transfer taxes apply when property is sold.","Escheat is for property without heirs.","","General taxes apply citywide."]'::jsonb, 'Special assessment: you benefit, you pay.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'special-assessment-example', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Property taxes are ad valorem, meaning they''re based on value.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Ad valorem means according to value."]'::jsonb, 'Ad valorem: by value.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'property-tax-ad-valorem', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Eminent domain can be used only for a public use or purpose.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Public use and just compensation are both required."]'::jsonb, 'Take it for the public, pay for it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'eminent-domain-public-use', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'A government dam project floods an owner''s land repeatedly, but the government never formally condemned it. The owner may sue for:', '["Partition","Inverse condemnation","Escheat","Specific performance"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Inverse condemnation lets an owner seek compensation when government action effectively takes property.', '["Partition is between co-owners.","","Escheat is for property without heirs.","Specific performance enforces contracts."]'::jsonb, 'Inverse: the owner starts the taking case.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'inverse-condemnation-example', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.1-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A new sidewalk costs $36 per front foot, split equally between the owner and the city. An owner has 80 front feet. What does the owner pay?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":1440,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Half of $2,880 is $1,440.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Special assessment: you benefit, you pay.', 'Owner cost = front feet × cost per foot × owner''s share', '["80 × $36 = $2,880 total.","Owner pays half: $2,880 × 0.5 = $1,440."]'::jsonb, null, 'special-assessment-frontage', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.2-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'An owner gets permission to build 3 feet closer to the side lot line than zoning allows, because the lot is oddly shaped. This is a:', '["Spot zoning","Conditional use permit","Nonconforming use","Variance"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'A variance permits deviation from zoning requirements because of hardship.', '["Spot zoning rezones a parcel.","A conditional use permit allows a special use, not a setback change.","A nonconforming use predates a zoning change.",""]'::jsonb, 'Variance bends the rule.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'variance-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N2.2-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N2', 'N2.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A gas station operating legally before its area was rezoned residential may continue as a:', '["Spot zone","Variance","Conditional use","Nonconforming use"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Uses that predate a zoning change are nonconforming and often allowed to continue.', '["Nothing was rezoned for one owner.","No variance was granted.","No special permit was needed; the use came first.",""]'::jsonb, 'Nonconforming came first.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'nonconforming-grandfathered', 'unverified'),
