  ('N4.3-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Which clause lets the lender demand the entire loan balance when the borrower defaults?', '["Alienation clause","Subordination clause","Defeasance clause","Acceleration clause"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Acceleration makes the full balance due on default.', '["Alienation is triggered by transfer, not default.","Subordination changes priority.","Defeasance requires release on payoff.",""]'::jsonb, 'Accelerate on default.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'acceleration-default', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.3-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A clause that makes the loan due in full if the property is sold is the:', '["Prepayment clause","Release clause","Alienation (due-on-sale) clause","Acceleration clause"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Alienation means transferring title; the clause triggers on sale.', '["Prepayment concerns paying early.","Release clauses free parcels from a blanket loan.","","Acceleration is about default generally."]'::jsonb, 'Alienate on sale.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'alienation-due-on-sale', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.3-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A buyer formally assumes the seller''s loan with the lender''s approval and a release of the seller. Who is liable on the loan?', '["The buyer","Both equally forever","The seller","Neither"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'With an assumption and release, the buyer becomes the one liable.', '["","With a release, the seller is off the hook.","The seller was released.","Someone always owes the debt."]'::jsonb, 'Assume it, own the debt.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'assumption-liability', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.3-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A buyer takes title subject to the seller''s existing loan. If the loan goes into default, the buyer:', '["Is personally liable for the full debt","Is unaffected","Could lose the property but isn''t personally liable for the debt","Can force the lender to sue only the seller and keep the house"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Subject-to buyers risk losing the property in foreclosure but aren''t personally liable; the seller remains liable.', '["That describes assumption.","The lender can still foreclose.","","The lender can foreclose on the property."]'::jsonb, 'Subject to it, don''t own the debt.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'subject-to-liability', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.3-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A landowner''s lender agrees that a construction lender''s loan will have first priority. This is done with a:', '["Release clause","Novation","Satisfaction","Subordination agreement"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Subordination lets one lien voluntarily take a lower priority.', '["A release frees property from a lien.","Novation replaces a contract.","A satisfaction shows a loan is paid off.",""]'::jsonb, 'Subordinate: step back in line.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'subordination-priority', 'unverified'),
