  ('N4.3-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'When a loan secured by a deed of trust is paid off, the trustee records a:', '["Lis pendens","Grant deed to the lender","Notice of default","Reconveyance"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Reconveyance returns title and clears the deed of trust.', '["A lis pendens is a lawsuit notice.","Title doesn''t go to the lender.","A notice of default starts foreclosure.",""]'::jsonb, 'Paid off: reconvey.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'reconveyance-payoff', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.3-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A loan has a prepayment penalty of 2% of the balance paid off early. The borrower pays off $185,000 early. How much is the penalty?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":3700,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '2% of $185,000 is $3,700.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Pay early, pay a penalty, if the note says so.', 'Penalty = balance prepaid × penalty rate', '["2% = 0.02.","$185,000 × 0.02 = $3,700."]'::jsonb, null, 'prepayment-penalty-calc', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.3-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'scenario', 3, 'application', 'A buyer proposes taking over your seller''s loan "subject to" without telling the lender. What should the agent do?', '["Explain the due-on-sale risk and that the seller stays liable, and recommend the seller get legal advice before agreeing","Promise the lender won''t find out","Encourage it as a quick way to close","Draft a side agreement yourself"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Subject-to deals keep the seller liable and can trigger due-on-sale. The seller needs legal advice.', '["","That''s a promise you can''t make, and it hides a material risk.","The seller could stay liable for a loan they no longer control.","Drafting legal agreements is the practice of law."]'::jsonb, 'Subject to it, the seller still owes.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-seller-wants-subject-to', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.4-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Which gives a seller the most confidence in a buyer''s financing?', '["An online calculator printout","The buyer''s word","A preapproval after the lender reviewed credit and documents","A prequalification based on what the buyer said"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Preapproval reflects a lender''s review of credit and documents.', '["Calculators verify nothing.","Unverified statements carry little weight.","","Prequalification isn''t verified."]'::jsonb, 'Prequal is a guess. Preapproval is checked.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'preapproval-vs-prequal', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.4-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A borrower earns $7,500 a month before taxes. Using a 28% housing ratio, what is the maximum monthly housing payment?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":2100,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '28% of $7,500 is $2,100.', '[]'::jsonb, '28 for the house, 36 for everything.', 'Maximum housing payment = gross monthly income × housing ratio', '["28% = 0.28.","$7,500 × 0.28 = $2,100."]'::jsonb, null, 'front-ratio-calc', 'unverified'),
  ('N4.4-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N4', 'N4.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'PRIN', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A borrower earns $9,000 a month. With a 36% total debt ratio and $900 in other monthly debts, what is the maximum housing payment?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":2340,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Total debts can be $3,240; subtracting $900 leaves $2,340 for housing.', '[]'::jsonb, '28 for the house, 36 for everything.', 'Max housing = (gross income × total ratio) − other debts', '["$9,000 × 0.36 = $3,240 total allowed.","$3,240 − $900 = $2,340."]'::jsonb, null, 'back-ratio-calc', 'unverified'),
