  ('S3.4-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'state', 'S3', 'S3.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'scenario', 3, 'application', 'A home inspector offers you $200 for each client you send. What should the agent do?', '["Accept, since inspectors aren''t lenders","Decline undisclosed compensation; any arrangement needs disclosure and your broker''s approval and must be legal","Accept and keep it private","Accept and tell the client after closing"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'No secret profits; disclose and follow your broker.', '["Undisclosed referral pay is a conflict of interest.","","Secret profit breaches duties.","Disclosure after the fact doesn''t fix it."]'::jsonb, 'No secret profit.', null, '[]'::jsonb, 'NRS 645.630 [verify citation]', 'nv-agent-gift-kickback', 'unverified'),
  ('S3.4-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'state', 'S3', 'S3.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Telling a buyer "this home will definitely be worth 30% more next year" is acceptable sales talk.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["A definite promise about future value is a false promise.",""]'::jsonb, 'Accurate, not hopeful.', null, '[]'::jsonb, 'NRS 645.630', 'nv-guarantee-future-value', 'unverified'),
  ('S3.4-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'state', 'S3', 'S3.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A broker can''t explain where a $4,000 deposit went. The likely violation is:', '["Steering","Blind advertising","Failing to account for money belonging to others","Unlicensed activity"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Brokers must account for others'' money.', '["Steering is a fair housing violation.","That''s about ads.","","The broker is licensed."]'::jsonb, 'Deposit it right, record it all.', null, '[]'::jsonb, 'NRS 645.630', 'nv-account-money-ground', 'unverified'),
  ('S3.4-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'state', 'S3', 'S3.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'A busy client asks to sign a blank offer form so you can fill it in later. What should the agent do?', '["Accept to save time","Accept but email them a copy later","Have a coworker sign for them","Decline; review and complete the terms with the client before they sign"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Clients sign completed documents they''ve reviewed.', '["Blank signatures invite misrepresentation.","A later copy doesn''t fix it.","Signing for someone is forgery.",""]'::jsonb, 'Fill it in, then sign.', null, '[]'::jsonb, 'NRS 645.630 [verify citation]', 'nv-agent-sign-blank-form', 'unverified'),
  ('S3.4-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'state', 'S3', 'S3.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'After a client signs a purchase agreement, a licensee generally must:', '["Provide copies of signed documents to the parties","Keep the only copy","Post it publicly","Send a copy to the Commission"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Parties get copies of what they sign.', '["","Parties are entitled to copies.","Contracts are confidential.","The Commission doesn''t collect contracts."]'::jsonb, 'Every signer gets a copy.', null, '[]'::jsonb, 'NRS 645.630 [verify citation]', 'nv-copies-to-parties', 'unverified'),
  ('S3.4-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'state', 'S3', 'S3.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'scenario', 3, 'application', 'You notice a coworker depositing client checks into their personal account. What should the agent do?', '["Ignore it; it''s not your client","Ask the coworker for a share","Report it to your broker right away","Wait until year-end to mention it"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The broker must act on possible commingling.', '["Client funds are at risk now.","That makes you part of it.","","Delay lets harm continue."]'::jsonb, 'Report it to your broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, 'NRS 645.630; NRS 645.310', 'nv-agent-coworker-commingling', 'unverified'),
  ('S3.4-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'state', 'S3', 'S3.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A licensee commits three separate violations. What is the maximum total administrative fine?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":30000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'Three violations at up to $10,000 each is $30,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Up to $10,000 per violation.', 'Total = violations × $10,000', '["Maximum per violation: $10,000.","3 × $10,000 = $30,000."]'::jsonb, 'NRS 645.630; NRS 645.633', 'nv-fine-calc-three', 'unverified')
